#: ../../adr/0024-procedures.md:1
msgid "ADR-0024: Procedures, declarative sequences of actions and measurements"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0024-procedures.md:3
msgid "**Status**: accepted"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0024-procedures.md:4
msgid "**Date**: 2026-10-20"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0024-procedures.md:5
msgid "**Plan step**: P15.11 (also P15.12, P15.13)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0024-procedures.md:7
msgid "Context"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0024-procedures.md:9
msgid ""
"A bench is used through *procedures*: close the shutter, take twenty "
"frames, average them into a dark, open the shutter, take ten frames and "
"subtract the dark. Such a sequence of actions and measurements in time, "
"whose intermediate results are reused, is neither the graph (a "
"computation), nor a study (sweep, Monte-Carlo, loop), nor a recorded "
"sequence of commands (ADR-0014, no measurement nor processing). The "
"review of 19/10/2026 and its decisions of 20/10 "
"(`docs/specs/pistes_evolution.md`, §3) ask for procedures built with "
"blocks in the web interface (Blockly), run by the service as jobs, "
"identical in simulation and in operation, usable as the body of a study, "
"and never running user code on the public instance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0024-procedures.md:17
msgid "Decision"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0024-procedures.md:19
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**A procedure is data.** A JSON object `{\"name\", \"description\", "
"\"steps\": [...]}`; each step is an object whose `do` names its kind. No "
"code, no expression language, no import: a procedure can only call what "
"the engine lists."
msgstr ""

