#: ../../adr/0024-procedures.md:37
msgid ""
"Values are quantities written as strings (`\"2 mm\"`), numbers, booleans,"
" strings or `\"$name\"`. The processing functions are a fixed table "
"(`mean`, `median`, `sum`, `stack`, `subtract`, `subtract_dark`, `divide`,"
" `scale`, `flat_field`, `crop`, `rebin`, `aperture_photometry`, `total`, "
"`maximum`...), each with its arguments; a plugin cannot extend it from a "
"document."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0024-procedures.md:41
msgid ""
"**Validation before any run** (`Procedure.problems(ctx)`): every element,"
" port, action, target, function and argument exists; every named result "
"is defined before it is used; loops are bounded (at most `MAX_ITERATIONS`"
" iterations in all, 10 000, before the run starts when the counts are "
"literal); nesting depth at most 16. The validation of the context reports"
" the problems of its procedures."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0024-procedures.md:45
msgid ""
"**Engine** `lumos.core.procedure`: `Procedure` (from and to JSON), "
"`run_procedure(ctx, procedure, *, progress, cancelled, confirm)` "
"returning a `ProcedureResult` (named results, values shown, journal of "
"the steps with their times). The context runs the graph for `measure`, "
"performs actions for `action`, advances its clock for `wait`; everything "
"is journaled with the origin of the run. `ctx.procedures` holds the "
"procedures of a context by name; the `.lumos` context document stores "
"them under `\"procedures\"` (format 1.3), and a procedure alone is a "
"document of kind `\"procedure\"`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0024-procedures.md:51
msgid ""
"**Service**: `set_procedure`, `remove_procedure`, `list_procedures`, "
"`run_procedure` (a job of kind `procedure`: progress, cancellation "
"between steps, journal, `max_run_seconds` and the other quotas; its named"
" results are the outputs of the job, read with `get_result`); the web API"
" and the MCP server expose the same operations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0024-procedures.md:55
msgid ""
"**Operation**: a procedure acting on equipment needs one human "
"confirmation for the whole run, listing the devices it drives "
"(`run_procedure(..., confirmed=True)`); without it the run is refused, as"
" a single action is (ADR-0014, ADR-0016)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0024-procedures.md:58
msgid ""
"**Python**: a procedure exports to an equivalent Python script (P15.12); "
"the *script mode* (a Python script instead of blocks) runs only on local "
"and private instances, never on the public one (P15.12, P15.4)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0024-procedures.md:60
msgid ""
"**Studies** (P15.13): a procedure may be the body of a sweep or a Monte-"
"Carlo run, its named results being the outputs of each point."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0024-procedures.md:63
msgid "Amendment (P15.12): script mode and export"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0024-procedures.md:65
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"`Procedure.to_python()` exports the steps; a procedure `{\"name\", "
"\"script\"}` is the script mode, run by `exec` with `ctx`, `results`, "
"`u`, `np` and `call` only when the service has `scripts_enabled`: true by"
" default on the local profile, false on the public one, where the "
"configuration refuses it unless `anonymous_role = \"none\"` (a private "
"instance whose visitors all log in). Loading a document never runs a "
"script. The web interface edits the steps with Blockly (13.3, "
"Apache-2.0), loaded only in the Procedures tab; the blocks are converted "
"to and from the JSON of the procedure by pure functions "
"(`web/src/lib/procedures.ts`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0024-procedures.md:72
msgid "Alternatives considered"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0024-procedures.md:74
msgid ""
"**A Python subset or an expression language in the documents**: flexible,"
" but it is code; a document could then compute anything, which the public"
" instance must refuse, and its sandboxing is a known source of "
"vulnerabilities."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0024-procedures.md:77
msgid ""
"**Procedures as graphs**: the graph describes a computation without time;"
" a procedure is ordered in time (actions, waits) with state (named "
"results), which a list of instructions shows directly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0024-procedures.md:79
msgid ""
"**Reusing recorded sequences** (ADR-0014): they replay commands only, "
"without measurement, processing nor control flow."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0024-procedures.md:82
msgid "Consequences"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0024-procedures.md:84
msgid ""
"Procedures run identically in Python, in the web interface and through "
"the MCP server, and are saved with their context."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0024-procedures.md:86
msgid ""
"The table of processing functions is the vocabulary of the procedures: "
"adding a function is a change of LUMOS (with its tests), not of a "
"document."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0024-procedures.md:88
msgid ""
"The Blockly editor (P15.12) only edits this JSON, which keeps the blocks "
"and the engine independent."
msgstr ""

